note Allen's first-visit greeting on aienos.com: the consent aside that every page carries.
note Every structural decision lives here: the section order, the ids and aria attributes the
note consent script (public/js/allen-intro.js) and its tests depend on, Drake's greeting words, the
note memory links kept apart from the X pixel buttons, the GPC note, the reply after No thanks, and
note the local-only "Who can see me right now?" panel. The script only toggles and fills these slots.
note
note Program mode. check.sh compiles this with the pinned omc shared with om/hive-page, runs it twice,
note and commits intro.html with its sha256. The Rust site builder embeds intro.html and re-hashes it
note in a unit test, so x86 CI checks the artifact without running the arm64 compiler.
note
note Allen's speech carries data-speaker="allen": his "we" means Allen and the visitor, and the
note site's singular-voice verifier exempts exactly those elements. Memory consent is links to
note /allen/?mode=remember and ?mode=anonymous; X consent is the Say hi and No thanks buttons. One tap
note never means both. Names: at most 8 bytes per data name.

note ihead: Host aside, avatar, name and close: closing means No.
text ihead "<aside id=\"aien-allen-intro\" role=\"complementary\" aria-label=\"Allen says hello\" aria-live=\"polite\" hidden><img class=\"allen-intro-avatar\" src=\"/assets/allen-avatar.svg\" alt=\"\" width=\"48\" height=\"48\"><div class=\"allen-intro-bubble\"><p class=\"allen-intro-name\">Allen</p><button id=\"allen-intro-close\" class=\"allen-intro-close\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"Close, no thanks\">×</button>"

note igreet: Drake's greeting as Allen says it. The ghost reserves the size; JS types into allen-intro-typed.
text igreet "<p id=\"allen-intro-message\" class=\"allen-intro-message\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-speaker=\"allen\"><span class=\"allen-intro-ghost\"><strong id=\"allen-intro-title\">Hey, I'm Allen. It's nice to meet you!</strong> <span id=\"allen-intro-intro\">You don't have to tell me your name, but if you do, that would be super awesome and we could chat over time. When you come back, I can remember who you are and we can pick up where we left off. We can talk about all kinds of good things in the universe.</span></span><span id=\"allen-intro-typed\"><strong></strong><span></span></span></p><p id=\"allen-intro-spoken\" class=\"allen-intro-sr\"></p>"

note ichat: Memory consent: plain links to /allen/, never the X pixel.
text ichat "<div id=\"allen-intro-chat\" class=\"allen-intro-chips\"><a href=\"/allen/?mode=remember\">Tell Allen my name</a><a href=\"/allen/?mode=anonymous\">Chat anonymously</a></div>"

note ixask: The X pixel ask, its own line and its own buttons.
text ixask "<div id=\"allen-intro-x\"><p id=\"allen-intro-offer\" class=\"allen-intro-note\" data-speaker=\"allen\">Separately, if you'd like, say hi and I'll let Drake know you stopped by. That uses Drake's X pixel to note the visit. Totally fine if not.</p><div id=\"allen-intro-chips\" class=\"allen-intro-chips\"><button id=\"allen-intro-yes\" type=\"button\">Say hi</button><button id=\"allen-intro-no\" type=\"button\">No thanks</button></div></div>"

note igpc: Shown instead of the X ask when the browser sends Global Privacy Control.
text igpc "<p id=\"allen-intro-gpc\" class=\"allen-intro-note\" data-speaker=\"allen\" hidden>Your browser sends Global Privacy Control, so I'm not offering Drake's X pixel. It stays off.</p>"

note iafter: After No thanks: no pixel, no memory, an anonymous chat.
text iafter "<div id=\"allen-intro-after\" hidden><p id=\"allen-intro-after-text\" data-speaker=\"allen\">No problem. You can still chat with me anonymously; I won't remember you or tell X anything.</p><p class=\"allen-intro-links\"><a id=\"allen-intro-anon\" href=\"/allen/?mode=anonymous\">Chat anonymously</a></p></div>"

note iwho: Local-only panel; filled from resource timing and navigator fields, never sent.
text iwho "<details id=\"allen-intro-who\" class=\"allen-intro-who\"><summary>Who can see me right now?</summary><div class=\"allen-intro-who-body\"><h3>Trackers on this page right now: <span id=\"allen-intro-tracker-count\">checking</span></h3><ul id=\"allen-intro-trackers\"></ul><p id=\"allen-intro-trackers-none\" hidden>None. Only this site's own files have loaded in this tab.</p><h3>What your browser tells every website automatically</h3><dl id=\"allen-intro-facts\"></dl><p>Every site you visit can see this. I don't keep it. Your IP address is visible to Drake's web host, like every site's.</p><h3>What this page can't see</h3><p>Trackers on other sites, in other tabs or inside embedded frames, tracking by your internet provider or network, and your browser extensions. Tools that check more:</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://coveryourtracks.eff.org/\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">EFF Cover Your Tracks</a></li><li><a href=\"https://themarkup.org/blacklight\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Markup's Blacklight</a></li></ul></div></details>"

note ifoot: Privacy link and the closing tags.
text ifoot "<p class=\"allen-intro-links\"><a href=\"/privacy/\">Privacy</a></p></div></aside>"

fn main to int
n = write 1 ihead 0 len ihead
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = write 1 igreet 0 len igreet
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = write 1 ichat 0 len ichat
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = write 1 ixask 0 len ixask
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = write 1 igpc 0 len igpc
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = write 1 iafter 0 len iafter
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = write 1 iwho 0 len iwho
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
n = write 1 ifoot 0 len ifoot
if lt n 0
trap 3
end
ret 0
end
